---
/**
 * /faq
 *
 * THE POINT OF THIS PAGE IS THAT THE STRUCTURED DATA IS GENERATED.
 *
 * The legacy page hand-wrote 14 accordions in HTML and hand-wrote a separate
 * FAQPage JSON-LD block beside them. They drifted: 9 questions in the schema
 * against 14 on screen, one answer truncated, two in a different order, and the
 * whole Security category — the most trust-critical block — absent from the
 * structured data entirely. 36% of the page was invisible to the consumers that
 * block exists for.
 *
 * Nobody did that on purpose. It is what two hand-maintained copies of the same
 * content guarantee over time. Here the accordions and the FAQPage node both
 * come from FAQ_CATEGORIES in src/data/faq.ts, so drift requires deleting one of
 * two call sites rather than merely forgetting.
 *
 * SEO is carried over verbatim: title, description, canonical.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../components/layout/Section.astro';
import Button from '../components/ui/Button.astro';
import { FAQ_CATEGORIES, FAQ_ALL } from '../data/faq';
import { faqPage, breadcrumbs } from '../lib/schema';

const title = 'FAQ | CrowAgent';
const description =
  'Plans, pricing, AI credits, security and the rules CrowMark reads. Answers to the questions UK bid teams ask most.';

const CALENDLY = 'https://calendly.com/crowagent-platform/30min';

/* Both nodes derive from the same array the page renders. */
const schema = [
  ...faqPage(FAQ_ALL),
  breadcrumbs([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'FAQ', path: '/faq' },
  ]),
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/faq" schema={schema}>
  <Section
    eyebrow="Help centre · Support"
    title="Questions about CrowAgent?"
    standfirst="Plans, pricing, AI credits, security and the rules CrowMark reads. If your question is not on this page, book a call."
    id="faq-top"
  
    as="h1">
    <div class="btn-row">
      <Button href={CALENDLY} target="_blank">Book a 30-minute call</Button>
      <Button href="#faq-general" variant="secondary">Browse questions</Button>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-search">
      <label class="faq-search__label" for="faq-search">Search the questions</label>
      <input
        class="field__input faq-search__input"
        id="faq-search"
        type="search"
        placeholder="Try &quot;credits&quot;, &quot;PPN&quot; or &quot;cancel&quot;"
        autocomplete="off"
      />
      {/* Politely announced, because a sighted reader watches the list shrink
          and a screen reader user is otherwise told nothing at all. */}
      <p class="faq-search__status" id="faq-search-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
    </div>
  </Section>

  {/*
    `joined` ON EVERY CATEGORY, INCLUDING THE FIRST (O-43). These are not five
    sections about five subjects; they are one register of questions broken into
    groups, and the reader scans down it. Rendered as plain adjacent sections
    each seam was a closing --sec-pad-y on top of an opening one: 171px at 1440
    between the last question of a group and the next group's eyebrow, against a
    ~60px rhythm inside the register itself. See Section.astro for the modifier
    and why it is a claim about the content rather than a rule about this page.

    The first one is joined to the hero for the same reason: the search field
    above it filters exactly this list, so the list continues from it.

    THE CLOSING SECTION BELOW IS NOT JOINED. "Still have questions?" stops
    answering and starts asking, and the full separation is what says so.
  */}
  {
    FAQ_CATEGORIES.map((cat) => (
      <Section eyebrow={cat.label} title={cat.heading} standfirst={cat.standfirst} id={cat.id} joined>
        <div class="faq-list">
          {cat.entries.map((e) => (
            <details class="faq-item" data-q={`${e.question} ${e.answer}`.toLowerCase()}>
              {/* No icon child: the mark is drawn by `summary::after` in
                  styles/blocks.css, on every disclosure on the site. This one
                  carried a hand-rolled 20px SVG chevron, one of four marks the
                  site drew for one job — and the fourth was nothing at all, on
                  the three legal routes. A-65. */}
              <summary class="faq-item__q">{e.question}</summary>
              <div class="faq-item__a">
                <p>{e.answer}</p>
                {e.link && (
                  <p>
                    <a href={e.link.href}>{e.link.label}</a>
                  </p>
                )}
              </div>
            </details>
          ))}
        </div>
      </Section>
    ))
  }

  <Section
    title="Still have questions?"
    standfirst="If the answer is not here, ask us directly. A person on the team that built it replies, usually within three to five business days."
    id="faq-contact"
  >
    {/*
      "EMAIL US" IS BACK (OA-28, 2026-08-02). faq.html:446-449 offers exactly two
      actions here, a Calendly booking and mailto:hello@crowagent.ai, and the port
      kept only the booking. The allow-list justified dropping the mailto by the
      "request access is a web form, never a bare mailto" rule, but that rule is
      about ACCESS REQUESTS, which this is not: it is the general enquiry address,
      already published on /contact in the hero and the directory. Losing it left
      a reader who does not want a form and does not want a call with nothing.
    */}
    <div class="btn-row">
      <Button href="/contact#contact-form">Send us a message</Button>
      <Button href={CALENDLY} variant="secondary" target="_blank">Book a call</Button>
      <Button href="mailto:hello@crowagent.ai" variant="secondary">Email us</Button>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Base>

<script>
  /**
   * Client-side filter. Deliberately hides the ANSWER-matching items too, not
   * just question matches: someone searching "credits" is as likely to be
   * looking for a phrase inside an answer.
   *
   * Everything is visible by default and the filter only ever REMOVES. If this
   * script never runs, the page is a complete, readable FAQ — which is the rule
   * that the earlier hide-then-reveal pattern on this site broke, leaving 4 of 9
   * homepage sections permanently invisible when an observer did not fire.
   */
  function initFaqSearch() {
    const input = document.getElementById('faq-search') as HTMLInputElement | null;
    const status = document.getElementById('faq-search-status');
    if (!input || !status) return;

    const items = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.faq-item'));
    const sections = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('section[id^="faq-"]'));
    if (!items.length) return;

    let timer: number | undefined;

    function apply() {
      const q = input!.value.trim().toLowerCase();
      let shown = 0;

      for (const item of items) {
        const hit = !q || (item.dataset.q ?? '').includes(q);
        item.hidden = !hit;
        if (hit) shown++;
        // Open matches once the query is specific enough to be worth reading,
        // and close them again when the query is cleared.
        if (q.length >= 3) (item as HTMLDetailsElement).open = hit;
        else if (!q) (item as HTMLDetailsElement).open = false;
      }

      // A category with nothing left in it is noise. Hide the whole section,
      // but never the hero or the closing block.
      for (const s of sections) {
        if (s.id === 'faq-top' || s.id === 'faq-contact') continue;
        const any = Array.from(s.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.faq-item')).some(
          (i) => !i.hidden
        );
        s.hidden = !any;
      }

      status!.textContent = q
        ? shown === 0
          ? `No questions match "${q}". Try a different term.`
          : `${shown} question${shown === 1 ? '' : 's'} match "${q}".`
        : '';
    }

    input.addEventListener('input', () => {
      window.clearTimeout(timer);
      timer = window.setTimeout(apply, 150);
    });

    // Enter would submit an enclosing form or reload; there is nothing to submit.
    input.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
      if ((e as KeyboardEvent).key === 'Enter') e.preventDefault();
    });
  }

  initFaqSearch();
</script>

<style>
  /* Centred to match the head block above it (owner decision, 2026-08-02).
     Alignment only: the row centres on the same axis as its heading. */

  .faq-search {
    /* ── CENTRED UNDER A CENTRED HEAD ─────────────────────────────────────
     *
     * A 460px block inside a full-measure container hugs the left edge unless
     * it is told not to. Measured at 1440: 302px left of the page centre, sitting
     * directly under a centred eyebrow, h1, standfirst and button pair, with
     * 600px of empty space to its right.
     *
     * Same defect as /compare's intro prose, and the same distinction applies:
     * the LABEL and the input's placeholder stay left-aligned because they are
     * read, while the BLOCK sits on the page's centre line like everything
     * above it. Where a column sits and how its text ragged-edges are two
     * different decisions. */
    margin-top: var(--sec-gap);
    max-width: 460px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .faq-search__label {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--t-body);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--c-text);
  }

  /* `.faq-search__input` WAS A BYTE-FOR-BYTE COPY of `.field__input` in
     styles/forms.css, 2026-08-04 — same width, same height, same padding, same
     border, same radius, same background, same face, same size. It is now the
     shared class in the markup and nothing is declared here. That copy is the
     clearest example on the site of why an accurate duplicate is still a defect:
     it was correct the day it was written and would have drifted the first time
     either file was touched. */

  .faq-search__input:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--c-interactive);
    outline-offset: 2px;
    border-color: var(--c-interactive);
  }

  .faq-search__status {
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--t-micro);
    color: var(--c-text-muted);
    min-height: 1em;
  }

  .faq-list { display: grid; }

  .faq-item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--c-border);
  }

  /* O-59: local `[hidden]` restatement removed — tokens.css owns it sitewide. */

  /* The flex, the gap, the pointer, `list-style: none` and the Safari marker
     rule all moved to `summary` in styles/blocks.css with the mark itself, A-65.
     What is left is this row's own size and type: it runs taller than the 44px
     shared floor because a question is a heading, and its rule is drawn by
     `.faq-item` above rather than by this element. */
  .faq-item__q {
    /* Comfortably over the WCAG 2.2 44px target floor. */
    min-height: 60px;
    padding: var(--stack-1) 0;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--t-h4);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.35;
    color: var(--c-text);
  }

  .faq-item__q:hover { color: var(--c-interactive); }

  .faq-item__q:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--c-interactive);
    outline-offset: 2px;
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* No auto margin here, so the block starts where the question does. The
     measure is doing its real job: capping the line length, not positioning
     the block.
   *
   * ── O-55 IS OPEN, AND IT IS NOT OPEN HERE ───────────────────────────────
   *
   * THE SENTENCE THAT USED TO FOLLOW SAID THIS BODY "belongs on the same left
   * edge as the question that opens it", AND IT DESCRIBED SOMETHING THAT HAS
   * NOT RENDERED SINCE styles/alignment.css LANDED. Measured on the built page:
   * both the question and this body compute `text-align: center`, inherited
   * from the sitewide rule on <main>. At 390 the longest answer sets sixteen
   * centred lines, each starting at a different x. The owner reported it.
   *
   * The fix is one line and it is NOT a local `text-align: left`, which the
   * whole point of that file is to refuse. It is this container joining the
   * "read rather than scanned" set in styles/alignment.css, alongside .prose,
   * .legal__body, .article-body, .gl-article and .cmp-body — a FAQ answer is
   * continuous body copy by exactly the test that file states.
   *
   * IT IS NOT MADE HERE BECAUSE THE GATE MIRRORS THAT LIST BY HAND. The BODIES
   * constant in scripts/check-render.js repeats the five selectors, and a sixth
   * in the stylesheet with no sixth in the gate fails the build — measured, with
   * the gate's own authority-walk replayed against this page: it reports
   * `div.faq-item__a`. check-render.js is owned by another agent this session,
   * so the stylesheet half is being held back rather than shipped broken. The
   * two edits are one line each and have to land together. */
  .faq-item__a {
    padding-bottom: var(--stack-2);
    max-width: 72ch;
  }

  .faq-item__a p {
    margin: 0 0 var(--stack-1);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: var(--t-body);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--c-text-sub);
  }

  .faq-item__a p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }

  .faq-item__a a {
    color: var(--c-interactive);
  }

  .faq-item__a a:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--c-interactive);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }
</style>
